  "id": "regression-discontinuity-design",
  "term": "regression-discontinuity design",
  "definition": "Regression-discontinuity design is a quasi-experimental research method used when random assignment is not practical or ethical, and it is presented as a useful alternative to a randomized controlled trial. In the health and psychology-related context of the packet, it is an established design that may also be adapted to analyze repeated measurements over time.",
